    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538-a1">

                <pb facs="0846" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg718"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    319.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Elduayen to Mr.
                            Foster</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of
                            State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#italic">Palace</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 5, 1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In reply to your note of the 31st of
                    March last, relative to the fine imposed on the captain of the American vessel
                    Ocean Pearl by the custom-house of Matanzas, I have the pleasure to make known
                    to your excellency that, as my colleague, the minister of ultramar, has informed
                    me, said fine in the part which belongs to the treasury has been remitted.</p>
                <p>I improve, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. ELDUAYEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
